      "description": "A non-invasive tool that turns a spiral drawn on a tablet into objective motor measures. Every point (x, y, pressure, time) becomes indices for severity, smoothness, speed, tremor, pressure, and consistency — and with an account each drawing is saved as a baseline, so subtle change surfaces session over session. Built on digitized spiral drawing, an established clinical method for characterizing upper-limb motor performance.",
